QUESTION: Q3 Best category by revenue
INTENT   : Aggregate item fact up to category
ASSUMPTION: Two-hop join items->products is safe: products has 1 row per product_id (verified 300 unique). LEFT JOIN keeps the 20 item lines with NULL product_id visible in an explicit '(no product_id)' bucket instead of silently dropping them. Category labels are RAW (16 variants) pending human approval of the canonical map.
SQL      :
SELECT COALESCE(p.category,'(no product_id)') AS category,
              ROUND(SUM(i.net_amount),0) AS revenue_vnd,
              COUNT(DISTINCT i.order_id) AS orders, SUM(i.quantity) AS units
       FROM order_items i LEFT JOIN products p ON p.product_id=i.product_id
       GROUP BY category ORDER BY revenue_vnd DESC
