QUESTION: Q5 Average order value
INTENT   : Money per order, not per line
ASSUMPTION: MUST divide by DISTINCT orders (a naive AVG(net_amount) over the item join would weight multi-line orders incorrectly). Assumption: only orders with payment_status='Paid' count as realized AOV.
SQL      :
WITH order_rev AS (
             SELECT i.order_id, SUM(i.net_amount) AS net
             FROM order_items i
             JOIN payments p ON p.order_id=i.order_id AND p.payment_status='Paid'
             GROUP BY i.order_id)
       SELECT ROUND(AVG(net),0) AS aov_vnd, COUNT(*) AS paid_orders FROM order_rev
RESULT   :
 aov_vnd  paid_orders
  1410.0        14997
VALIDATE : PASS - line-weighted AOV would be lower (~828); this per-order AOV = 1,410 matches EDA

